{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xom8m4siT2QaFdqxJHqThu","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/adr/0001-npm-installs-a-single-hermes-user-plugin.md:31:  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:146:`terminal` (back up first) or use `hermes config set`, then validate with\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:637:hermes config set cron.model \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\"\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:638:hermes config set cron.model_provider custom:tiiny\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:802:  `hermes config set KEY VAL` covers `config.yaml`; `~/.hermes/.env` has no\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:4:in Hermes config. Config is changed only through `hermes config set`:\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:21:- [ ] `install --configure` calls `hermes config set` for\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:23:- [ ] `install --configure` calls `hermes config set` for the `tiiny`\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:25:- [ ] `install --no-configure` makes no `hermes config set` call\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:27:      `hermes config set` call\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:29:- [ ] `install --configure` exits non-zero when `hermes config set`\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/spec.md:114:    revert config; it prints the `hermes config set` command to unselect\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/spec.md:125:- Config is changed only through `hermes config set`, never by editing\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/spec.md:165:  with it; `--configure` calls `hermes config set` for the backend and\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/09-uninstall.md:6:revert config; it prints the `hermes config set` command to unselect the\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/09-uninstall.md:22:- [ ] `uninstall` makes no `hermes config set` call\n# Ship as one Hermes user plugin directory, installed by npm\n\n**Status:** Accepted (2026-11-20)\n\n## Context\n\nThe routing backend, the controller and the skill are Python and Markdown\nthat run inside, or alongside, the Hermes harness. Before this decision they\nwere installed by hand into three places: the routing backend into the\nHermes source tree (wiped on every Hermes update), the controller into\n`~/.hermes/scripts/`, and the skill into a category folder under\n`~/.hermes/skills/`. The three copies drifted, and each side found the\nothers by searching a hardcoded list of paths.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe package is published to npm. Its installer copies one directory into\nthe Hermes user plugin directory (`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`).\nThat directory holds the routing backend, the controller and the skill. The\nrouting backend registers the skill itself through Hermes's plugin skill\nAPI, so nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. Every lookup between\nthe three is relative to that one directory.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **pip package.** Fits the runtime language, but Hermes runs in its own\n  Python environment and the controller runs on the system `python3`;\n  installing into the right interpreter is its own problem. npm gives a\n  zero-dependency `npx` installer that runs anywhere Node does.\n- **`hermes plugins install <git url>`.** Native, but it takes only git\n  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\n  `doctor`.\n- **Separate skill copy under `~/.hermes/skills/`.** Editable by agents in\n  place, but that is exactly how the copies drifted before.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- npm delivers Python. Node is an install-time dependency only.\n- The installed copy is a snapshot: upgrading the package means running\n  `install` again.\n- The skill is read-only and namespaced (`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`)\n  and disappears when the routing backend is disabled.\n- `uninstall` removes one directory.\nissues/\nlearnings.md\nprogress.md\nspec.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3379957-013e-4424-a9ef-97f5b46aaf7e","uuid":"7a2eef13-a173-4a3d-a5eb-8e12eac85f33","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:46:52.940Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/adr/0001-npm-installs-a-single-hermes-user-plugin.md:31:  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:146:`terminal` (back up first) or use `hermes config set`, then validate with\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:637:hermes config set cron.model \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\"\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:638:hermes config set cron.model_provider custom:tiiny\ntiiny-router/SKILL.md:802:  `hermes config set KEY VAL` covers `config.yaml`; `~/.hermes/.env` has no\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:4:in Hermes config. Config is changed only through `hermes config set`:\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:21:- [ ] `install --configure` calls `hermes config set` for\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:23:- [ ] `install --configure` calls `hermes config set` for the `tiiny`\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:25:- [ ] `install --no-configure` makes no `hermes config set` call\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:27:      `hermes config set` call\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/08-config-step.md:29:- [ ] `install --configure` exits non-zero when `hermes config set`\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/spec.md:114:    revert config; it prints the `hermes config set` command to unselect\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/spec.md:125:- Config is changed only through `hermes config set`, never by editing\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/spec.md:165:  with it; `--configure` calls `hermes config set` for the backend and\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/09-uninstall.md:6:revert config; it prints the `hermes config set` command to unselect the\n.scratch/hermes-plugin-package/issues/09-uninstall.md:22:- [ ] `uninstall` makes no `hermes config set` call\n# Ship as one Hermes user plugin directory, installed by npm\n\n**Status:** Accepted (2026-11-20)\n\n## Context\n\nThe routing backend, the controller and the skill are Python and Markdown\nthat run inside, or alongside, the Hermes harness. Before this decision they\nwere installed by hand into three places: the routing backend into the\nHermes source tree (wiped on every Hermes update), the controller into\n`~/.hermes/scripts/`, and the skill into a category folder under\n`~/.hermes/skills/`. The three copies drifted, and each side found the\nothers by searching a hardcoded list of paths.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe package is published to npm. Its installer copies one directory into\nthe Hermes user plugin directory (`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`).\nThat directory holds the routing backend, the controller and the skill. The\nrouting backend registers the skill itself through Hermes's plugin skill\nAPI, so nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. Every lookup between\nthe three is relative to that one directory.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **pip package.** Fits the runtime language, but Hermes runs in its own\n  Python environment and the controller runs on the system `python3`;\n  installing into the right interpreter is its own problem. npm gives a\n  zero-dependency `npx` installer that runs anywhere Node does.\n- **`hermes plugins install <git url>`.** Native, but it takes only git\n  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\n  `doctor`.\n- **Separate skill copy under `~/.hermes/skills/`.** Editable by agents in\n  place, but that is exactly how the copies drifted before.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- npm delivers Python. Node is an install-time dependency only.\n- The installed copy is a snapshot: upgrading the package means running\n  `install` again.\n- The skill is read-only and namespaced (`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`)\n  and disappears when the routing backend is disabled.\n- `uninstall` removes one directory.\nissues/\nlearnings.md\nprogress.md\nspec.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xom8m4siT2QaFdqxJHqThu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
