{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYuNR3CcJ9cHDq2rYRL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The config step is in and all six checklist items are done. `npm test` passes: 14 Node tests and 6 Python tests. There is no lint script.\n\n`install` now takes `--configure` or `--no-configure`, and runs the config step only after `hermes plugins validate` passes:\n\n1. With `--configure` it runs `hermes config set` for the `tiiny` provider block from `references/backend.md`, then for `delegation.backend` set to `tiiny-router`. The backend goes last so it is never selected without its provider. Afterwards it says the change takes effect from the next Hermes session.\n2. With `--no-configure` it makes no config calls.\n3. With neither flag, on a terminal it asks y/N. Without a terminal it changes nothing and prints the exact `hermes config set` commands to run by hand.\n4. If any `hermes config set` fails, it stops and exits non-zero. Settings applied before the failure stay applied, and the message says so.\n\nNothing reads or writes `config.yaml` or `.env` in any mode, and a test checks this for all three modes.\n\n**Main risk:** I couldn't confirm how `hermes config set` handles values. I assumed it reads them as YAML, so `262144` and `false` become a number and a boolean. The model ids contain dots, so `providers.tiiny.models` can't use dotted keys and is set as one JSON value instead. If Hermes stores values as plain strings, this needs another approach. Test it against a real Hermes before release.\n\n**Test coverage:**\n- **Tests that failed first:** the backend selection, the provider entries, and the failure exit code.\n- **Tests that passed without new code:** `--no-configure`, the no-flag run without a terminal, and the config-file check. For each I temporarily broke the code and saw it fail.\n- **No automated test:** the y/N prompt, because it needs a terminal. I checked it by hand under a Python pty: `y` made all 10 config calls and `n` made none.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- The first version of the prompt crashed with `EAGAIN`. Reading `process.stdin.isTTY` makes stdin non-blocking, so I check with `tty.isatty` instead.\n- In `references/backend.md` I added `models_discovered: false` to the provider block, since the text already said it matters but the block left it out.\n- `fallback_providers` (MiniMax) is not set, because it depends on each user's paid provider.\n- The test helper can now make only certain `hermes` calls fail (`hermesFailsOn`).\n- AGENTS.md now lists the model table in `src/config.ts` among the files to update when a tier model changes. It also covers the stdin problem and how to test the prompt by hand.\n\nThe `install` option parsing rejects unknown flags, so whichever ticket adds `--force` has to extend it. Notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`, uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1186,"cache_read_input_tokens":84994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1186},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3379957-013e-4424-a9ef-97f5b46aaf7e","uuid":"e6d1c681-6690-461f-81d9-ca89407b1179","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:51:10.436Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYuNFN7tx7RDtSt3i1x"}
